    <origin>Owner round 3b (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md:78-86): "a red notification banner on any record subject to a No Access restriction, linking to a No Access list modal" and "a red notification banner showing a record is secure, linking to Share/Manage Access if possible". Disposition row 3 and open question O1 (notes/session27-ux-research-ethical-wall-secure.md:69, :74).</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Show every person who opens a project, matter or work assignment, in the standard form banner, that the record is SECURE and/or that a No Access restriction applies to it; show the same kind of banner on an Organization or Contact form when No Access entries name that organization or contact. Add, inside TrackingFieldTrio, a clickable indicator that opens Manage Access at the right section. Both surfaces read ONE BFF summary that any reader of the record may call. When that summary cannot be obtained or any part of it is unknown, the form shows a neutral "access status unavailable" notice — never silence that reads as "not restricted".</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — BFF ExternalAccess read path and endpoint filters, classic form web resources over Spaarke.BffAuth, the TrackingFieldTrio PCF and its shared Fluent v9 core. Fail closed (ADR-003); the absence of a banner is itself a claim.</role>

  <goal>(1) 064's Read-gated `GET` No Access SUMMARY route, extended by this task with the Secure signal and a closed signal block, returns, for a project, matter, work assignment, organization or contact the CALLER can Read, a closed set of signals each in state `applies` / `doesNotApply` / `unknown`, echoing the record id, with no entry ids, subject or object names and no reasons. (2) A thin on-load/post-save web resource on the five main forms maps those states to fixed red (ERROR) notifications, and maps any `unknown`, a non-200 response, a missing auth helper or a thrown call to one neutral INFO "access status unavailable" notification. (3) TrackingFieldTrio renders a Secure / No Access / unavailable indicator in its header row; for a caller the server says may manage access, clicking it opens AccessGrantModal through 067's section plumbing, at the No Access section (No Access) or at the top, Current Access (Secure); for everyone else it is a non-clickable indicator with a tooltip. (4) A live manual gate proves the banner on all five forms, under 150's field-level security, for a Read-only user and a Write user.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHAT THE OWNER ASKED (round 3b, BINDING; session27 note :78-86). A red banner on any record subject to a No Access restriction, linking to the No Access list; a red banner showing a record is secure, linking to Share/Manage Access if possible. The research note (session27-ux-research-ethical-wall-secure.md) assigns the indicator to this task (disposition row 3) and leaves O1 open (:74): the standard form banner is text-only, so a clickable indicator has to live inside TrackingFieldTrio.

WHAT EXISTS TODAY (verified 2026-10-01 against this branch).
- No authored code calls `setFormNotification` or `addNotification`: a Grep of src/ (node_modules excluded) matches only compiled PCF artifacts (`src/client/pcf/*/Solution/Controls/**/bundle.js`, 9 files). There is no on-form access signal except the header Owner and one line inside the Manage Access modal (`AccessGrantModal.tsx:1170-1178`, "Secure record — Owner … · Business Unit …").
- The modal's designed banner states are Fluent v9 `MessageBar intent="error"` with `MessageBarTitle` (`AccessGrantModal.tsx:1145-1168`: Restricted, then the delegation/auth deny state). That is the visual precedent for a red access state.
- TrackingFieldTrio (shared core) renders its governance icons in the header row: `TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:253-287` (person icon "Grant access" `:256-273`, email icon `:274-285`), placed by `:297-302`. The person icon is enabled only when `canGrantAccess === true` (`:248`, task 118 fail-closed). Props contract: `TrackingFieldTrio/types.ts:26-93` (`onOpenGrantModal` `:71`, `canGrantAccess` `:92`). Existing consumers that do not pass the governance props see no toolbar (`types.ts:59-66`); the email reading pane is one such consumer.
- The PCF host (`src/client/pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts`) binds to project, matter and work assignment (`GRANT_ROOT_BY_ENTITY` `:211-213`, `resolveGrantRoot()` `:459`). It asks the server whether the caller may manage access (`evaluateGrantGate()` `:594-657`: `GET /api/v1/external-access/can-manage-access`, every non-200 or unexpected body → false, the answer must echo THIS record id via `normalizeRecordId` `:639-648`, stale answers dropped by `setGrantGate` `:669-676`). That is the pattern this task's status fetch copies. The modal is opened by `onOpenGrantModal` (`:1102-1105`) and mounted with its props at `:1170-1207`. The host renders under a hard-coded `webLightTheme` (`:1135`). Its `fetchSecureOwnerInfo` (`:945-963`) reads `sprk_issecure` in user context and returns null on ANY failure — fail-soft by design for a display line, so it must NOT become the banner's source.
- SERVER. The `/api/v1/external-access` management group (`ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:123-126`) carries `DelegationRuleFilter`, whose required right is Write (`DelegationRuleFilter.cs:86`, check `:170-179`). `can-manage-access` (`RecordAccessGateEndpoint.cs:63-108`) answers the Write question and says of itself that it is not a permissions API and must not become one (`:27-32`). A Read-only viewer therefore cannot get a status from any route on that group, and a banner built on it would be blank for exactly the people who most need it.
- The root-flag reader cannot express "unknown". `ExternalParticipationService.GetRootRecordFlagsAsync` (`:541-624`) maps a row to `IsSecure: row.sprk_issecure == true` (`:605`), so a masked or NULL flag reads NOT secure, and maps an unreadable/unreturned row to `RootRecordFlags.Unreadable` = secure AND restricted (`ExternalCallerContext.cs:149`). Both are correct for a VETO and both are wrong for a banner: one would hide a secure record's banner, the other would show "SECURE" on a record nobody could read. Task 138 is adding a Limited signal to the same struct (`ExternalCallerContext.cs:139-153`).
- The deny reader answers only "which of these candidate records is this SUBJECT denied" (`NoAccessListReader.cs:128-155`; select list `:180-182`; subject filter `:191-206`; object filters `:209-222`; `GetDeniedRecordsAsync` `:268`). It has no record-scoped or subject-scoped listing. Task 064's UX amendment (`tasks/064-provenance-read-and-denylist-endpoints.poml`, amendment n="UX", lines 111-144) now owns ALL of it:
  - a record-scoped method on `NoAccessListReader` (064 RULES "Reuse, do not fork");
  - for a root record, its own entries plus organization walls over its referenced organizations (064 items (1)-(2));
  - for an sprk_organization record, entries naming it as subject or object organization; for a contact, entries naming it as subject contact plus entries whose subject organization is one of its ACTIVE organizations (064 item (3));
  - a SUMMARY tier route OUTSIDE the Write-gated group, gated on the caller's Read through `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` with one new Read-mapped `OperationAccessPolicy` key (064 "Authorization"), returning "whether any active entry applies, and counts by subject kind and by object path", with no Reason and no subject identities (064 item "SUMMARY block");
  - fail closed: any read fault returns ProblemDetails, never an empty or negative summary (064 RULES);
  - 064 itself says STOP and escalate before widening the shared entity-set map for the organization summary (064 "Authorization", last bullet).
  The SUMMARY route carries no Secure signal; adding it, and the closed signal block both clients read, is this task's server work.
- Record-side organizations for a wall: `GetReferencedOrganizationIdsAsync` (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:710`) over `sprk_assignedlawfirm1/2` (`:661-667`), returning `Unreadable` per record on a fault. A contact's active organizations: `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync` (`:1081`).
- Per-record caller rights: `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync` (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:210`), which collapses every "could not answer" into `AccessRights.None`. The route-keyed gate 064 reuses is `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:24-35` registration with an operation key, `:124-232` decision). Three facts constrain it here:
  - its insufficient-rights 403 copy is upload-specific ("You do not have permission to add content to this record.", `:221-224`);
  - it resolves entity sets ONLY through `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:167`), and its own remarks forbid a map of its own ("there were already three in the codebase before task 076 and a fourth is a review failure", `:58-63`);
  - that shared map (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:123-147`) has `contact` (`:123`) but no `sprk_organization`, and carries a LOCKSTEP INVARIANT with `DocumentAssociationMap` (`:111-122`). `DocumentAssociationMap` has no organization entry (Grep of `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse` for "organization" in `DocumentAssociationMap*.cs`: no match), so adding `sprk_organization` to the shared map would authorize document filing to organizations that can never be associated.
  So the Organization banner's read gate is an open design tension (escalation (f)), not a choice this task makes alone.
- AUTH SCHEME. A CIAM token cannot reach the workforce-default `/api/v1/external-access` group (`AuthorizationModule.cs:334-343`). The new route is workforce-only in the same way.
- WEB RESOURCE PATTERNS. On-load + `Spaarke.BffAuth`: `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_matter_kpi_refresh.js` (header `:1-29`). `addOnPostSave`: `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:160-215`. The auth helper's file is `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_bff_auth.js`; its WEB RESOURCE NAME, the one registered on forms, is `sprk_/scripts/bff_auth.js` (`:4`, `:20-25`). Token: `getToken` (`:178`) and `authenticatedFetch` (`:234`).
  - ⚠️ `getToken` never throws and never prompts: on a cold cache or any failure it resolves `null` (`:45-46`, `:172-221`), and `authenticatedFetch` then resolves `null` WITHOUT calling fetch (`:226-239`). A null token or a null Response is therefore a normal outcome that this task must render as "unavailable".
  - ⚠️ `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:282-293` SKIPS the call when the helper is absent or the token is null — fail-soft, correct for a KPI recalculation and wrong for a banner.
- FORM NOTIFICATION MECHANISMS (O1 is under owner investigation, research note :75-77; findings in the researcher's memory `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/mda-clickable-form-banner-options-2026-09-30.md`, Microsoft Learn sources listed there, NOT repo-verified):
  - `formContext.ui.setFormNotification(message, level, uniqueId)` — documented text-only, form-scoped, leaves with the form. An undocumented fourth "actions" parameter exists (community only, UNSUPPORTED; do not use).
  - `Xrm.App.addGlobalNotification({ type: 2, level, message, action: { actionLabel, eventHandler } })` — the only documented banner with a clickable action. It is APP-wide, not form-scoped, persists across in-app navigation, and there is no form unload event to clear it. Repo precedent without an action: `src/client/webresources/js/sprk_registrationribbon.js:270-282`. Its handler runs in the web resource's context and cannot open AccessGrantModal, which lives inside the TrackingFieldTrio PCF (`index.ts:1170-1207`).
  - `control.addNotification` (RECOMMENDATION is the only clickable level and is not red), `appnotification` (per-user bell/toast, not record-scoped) and Power Fx `Notify` (no action, cannot fire on form load) do not fit. ⚠️ `.claude/constraints/webresource.md` "Authentication" still says web-resource-called endpoints must be `.AllowAnonymous()`; that section predates `Spaarke.BffAuth` (task 030 / FR-17) and is superseded by it. Do not follow it here (CLAUDE.md §9: every endpoint requires auth).
- After 150, `sprk_issecure` is field-secured with Read granted to every user and to the BFF app identity (150 goal (1), constraint "None may be masked"). A masked read is therefore a configuration fault, and this task must render it as unknown, not as "not secure".
- A masked attribute and a stored NULL come back the same way from a Web API read (null or absent), so the Secure read cannot tell them apart. Rows whose `sprk_issecure` is NULL (for example rows that predate the column) would therefore show "Access status unavailable" permanently. Step 1 counts them live; escalation (g) applies if any exist.
- Opening the OOB Share dialog from a banner is not recommended (research note :59: no supported API, and it would bypass task 139's grantor cap and task 143's guard). Manage Access is the target.</background>
