  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 fail closed (owner directive)">Scope: the endpoint, the web resource and the TrackingFieldTrio indicator. Each signal is exactly one of `applies`, `doesNotApply`, `unknown`.
- Server: a fault, timeout, non-success status, missing row, masked/NULL `sprk_issecure`, `RootRecordFlags.Unreadable`, `ReferencedOrganizations.Unreadable`, a `NoAccessListResult.FailedClosed` result, or an unreadable organization membership makes THAT signal `unknown`. Never `doesNotApply`, and never `applies` (an unreadable record is not evidence that it is secure).
- 064's rule stands: a fault in the No Access read returns ProblemDetails for the whole request, never a 200 with a negative signal. Inside a 200, a signal is `unknown` only where that one signal could not be established while the others could (e.g. a masked or NULL Secure flag).
- Client: a non-200 (including 403 and 404), an unparseable body, a body whose recordId does not name this record (compare through `normalizeRecordId`), a missing `Spaarke.BffAuth`, an unresolved BFF base URL, a `null` token or `null` Response from `Spaarke.BffAuth.authenticatedFetch` (`sprk_bff_auth.js:226-239`), or a thrown call renders the unavailable notice. A signal kind missing from the body, or an unrecognised state value, is `unknown`.
- `doesNotApply` renders NOTHING for that signal; no surface ever prints "not secure", "not restricted" or similar.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 3b + O2 (disclosure)">Scope: the summary response and every string rendered from it. The response carries no entry ids, no subject or object ids or names, no reasons and no per-entry enforcement detail. The counts 064's SUMMARY block defines (by subject kind and by object path) may remain in the payload as 064 specifies; this task adds no other field beyond the signal block, the Secure signal and the record-id echo, and NEITHER client renders a count. The No Access list itself stays behind Manage Access (064's entries tier + 067, Write) and the NO ACCESS sections (154, access administrators per O2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-003 (read-tier gate)">Scope: the summary route. The gate is 064's: the caller must hold Read on the named record, evaluated as the caller over OBO through `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync`, in `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` with 064's Read-mapped `OperationAccessPolicy` key, before the handler runs. This task adds no filter and no operation key.
- Every "could not answer" is a 403 ProblemDetails (ADR-019, stable reason code, trace id). Write is NOT required.
- The 403 detail must not say "add content": if 064 shipped with the upload copy (`RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:221-224`), make that detail operation-specific, with the upload routes' text unchanged.
- The route is not on the `/api/v1/external-access` adminGroup (`ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:123-126`), is workforce-scheme only (a CIAM token is refused, as at `AuthorizationModule.cs:334-343`), and is never `.AllowAnonymous()`.
- Entity sets: project, matter, work assignment and contact resolve through `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:167`). `sprk_organization` follows escalation (f): neither the shared map nor a route-local map is added without that resolution.
- Any other entity type → 403. Never a 400, and never a pass-through.</constraint>
    <constraint source="closed signal set">Scope: the DTO, both clients and the tests. Every No Access kind is derived from 064's record-scoped read (its items (1)-(3)); this task only maps that result to kinds and states. Per entity type the response carries exactly these kinds, always all of them:
- sprk_project / sprk_matter / sprk_workassignment: `secure`; `noAccessOnRecord` = an active entry whose object record is this record, OR whose object organization is one of this record's referenced organizations (`GetReferencedOrganizationIdsAsync`).
- sprk_organization: `organizationDenied` (active entry with `sprk_subjectorganization` = this organization) and `organizationWall` (active entry with `sprk_objectorganization` = this organization).
- contact: `contactDenied` (active entry with `sprk_subjectcontact` = this contact) and `contactMemberOfDeniedOrganization` (active entry whose subject organization is one of this contact's ACTIVE organizations, via `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync`).
Only ACTIVE entries count (`statecode eq 0`, as `CombineFilter` does at `NoAccessListReader.cs:233-234`). A malformed entry (Business Rule 1 of the schema doc) counts for `noAccessOnRecord` exactly as the reader treats it: it denies nothing, so it does not make the signal `applies`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 — one composer, one route">Scope: server. Every No Access signal comes from 064's record-scoped read; the Secure signal is one added single-row read in 064's composer. This task adds no endpoint file, no route, no method on `NoAccessListReader`, no second deny reader and no second HTTP reader of `sprk_noaccessentries`. It extends 064's SUMMARY route and DTO. If 064 merged without that route, or without item (3) (organization and contact records), escalation (c) applies; this task does not build a substitute. Do not add sprk_noaccessentry columns to `NoAccessListReader.RowSelect` (`:180-182`): a column missing in an environment turns every deny read into a fail-closed outage.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner R3/R4 — minutes, not hours">Scope: server. The summary is computed per request (no new cache, the 064 "compute, don't store" rule). A change to an entry or to the Secure flag shows on the next form load or refresh.</constraint>
    <constraint source="the Secure signal">Scope: server. Read `sprk_issecure` app-only for the one record and keep three outcomes: true → `applies`; false → `doesNotApply`; absent, NULL, unreadable or unreturned → `unknown`. Do not derive it from `RootRecordFlags` as it stands (`ExternalCallerContext.cs:139-153`). If task 138 or 150 has added a readability discriminator to that struct or to `GetRootRecordFlagsAsync`, use it; otherwise read the single row in the composer. Do not change `GetRootRecordFlagsAsync`'s veto semantics. Never map NULL to `doesNotApply`, even where NULL is a legacy value: NULL rows are handled by escalation (g), not by the read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="banner copy (closed set — proposed, confirmed under escalation O1)">Scope: sprk_accessstatus_banner.js. Use exactly these notifications, with fixed unique ids. Each is cleared when its signal is not `applies`.
- `secure` (level ERROR, id `sprk_access_secure`): "SECURE RECORD — only people given access explicitly can see this record. People who can manage access see and change who has access in Manage Access (the person icon in the tracking panel)."
- `noAccessOnRecord` (ERROR, id `sprk_access_noaccess`): "NO ACCESS RESTRICTION — named people or organizations are blocked from this record. People who can manage access see the list in Manage Access › No Access (the person icon in the tracking panel)."
(The copy names who can act, because the person icon is disabled for a caller without Write, `TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:248`, `:267`; it must not tell a Read-only viewer to click something they cannot.)
- `organizationDenied` (ERROR, id `sprk_access_org_denied`): "NO ACCESS — this organization is on the No Access list: its active members are blocked from specific records. Access administrators manage the entries in the NO ACCESS section."
- `organizationWall` (ERROR, id `sprk_access_org_wall`): "ETHICAL WALL — named people or organizations are blocked from every record that references this organization. Access administrators manage the entries in the NO ACCESS section."
- `contactDenied` (ERROR, id `sprk_access_contact_denied`): "NO ACCESS — this contact is on the No Access list and is blocked from specific records. Access administrators manage the entries in the NO ACCESS section."
- `contactMemberOfDeniedOrganization` (ERROR, id `sprk_access_contact_org_denied`): "NO ACCESS — this contact belongs to an organization on the No Access list, so it is blocked wherever that organization is."
- Any `unknown`, or any client failure (INFO, id `sprk_access_unavailable`): "Access status unavailable — whether this record is secure or under a No Access restriction could not be checked. Do not assume it is unrestricted; reload the form to try again."
The owner's O1/O2 answers may revise this wording; implement the revised wording verbatim. Do not compose other strings.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-006 / webresource.md / §6.5 path C">Scope: sprk_accessstatus_banner.js. A form event handler (permitted for web resources), thin: no rule evaluation in the browser. The server decides each state; the script maps a state to a fixed string.
- `"use strict"`, `Spaarke.AccessStatus` namespace, every handler wrapped in try/catch, and the form never breaks.
- Registered on the main form of each of the five tables, after `sprk_/scripts/bff_auth.js`. Events: OnLoad, `formContext.data.addOnLoad` (re-run after a data refresh, e.g. 142's and 150's ribbon commands call `formContext.data.refresh(false)`, 142 POML :319), and `addOnPostSave`. Handlers are added once per form load, not once per event.
- Each evaluation first clears all seven notification ids, then shows the result. A late answer for a record the form has left, or an answer older than a newer evaluation, is dropped.
- No call on a create form with no record id. Main forms only, not quick-create forms.
- Do NOT copy the fail-soft skip at `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:282-293`: a missing helper, a `null` token or a `null` Response shows the unavailable notice.
- Superseded rule: `.claude/constraints/webresource.md` (`:34`, `:41-47`) says web-resource-called endpoints MUST be `.AllowAnonymous()`. That rule predates `Spaarke.BffAuth` and contradicts CLAUDE.md §9; it does not apply. Use `Spaarke.BffAuth.authenticatedFetch`. (Fixing that constraint file is the main session's job; `.claude/` is outside this task.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="O1 (escalation) — TrackingFieldTrio indicator">Scope: TrackingFieldTrio.tsx/types.ts and the PCF index.ts.
- ONE new opt-in prop, `accessStatus` (the closed signal states, or an explicit unavailable value). The click reuses 067's section-aware `onOpenGrantModal(section?)`; no second open callback is added. A consumer that does not pass `accessStatus` renders exactly as today; the email reading pane is unchanged. The indicator is clickable only when `onOpenGrantModal` is also supplied.
- Rendered in the header row beside the governance icons (`:297-302`).
- States: Secure and/or No Access shown in red, using `tokens.colorPaletteRedBackground2` (the palette already used at `:72-76`) with `tokens.colorNeutralForeground1` text. Unavailable shown neutral (`tokens.colorNeutralForeground3`), never red and never absent. Nothing is shown when every signal is `doesNotApply`.
- Clickable ONLY when `canGrantAccess === true` (`:248`): a No Access click opens AccessGrantModal at 067's No Access section; a Secure click opens it with no section, i.e. at the top (Current Access), as the person icon does. When both apply, the click targets No Access. Otherwise no handler is attached, and a tooltip says the caller cannot manage access here — the same discipline as the person icon (`:256-273`). The unavailable state is never clickable.
- The PCF fetches the summary with `evaluateGrantGate`'s rules (`index.ts:594-676`): fail closed, record-id echo, stale answers dropped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / ADR-022 / pcf.md">Scope: all UI touched. Fluent v9 semantic tokens only, no hard-coded colours, icons via `currentColor`. React 16-safe primitives in the shared core (the header comment `TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:28-32`); PCF platform libraries are not bundled. The PCF host's `webLightTheme` (`index.ts:1135`) is not changed by this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugin, flow or service endpoint. No Dataverse test in CI: live proof is the MANUAL gate, using existing non-admin test users in their current BUs (no relocation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement statement against `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (extension of 064's summary route in BFF; no new endpoint, service or package). Publish size: fresh-master vs fresh-branch worktrees at short paths, Compress-Archive, both sizes, delta and both file counts, ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE. Tests under tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ for the reader/composer change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests. Use the reader's `QueryChunkAsync` override seam and the participation-service subclass seam (`GetRootRecordFlagsAsync`/`GetReferencedOrganizationIdsAsync` are virtual).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>(1) Endpoint: the only per-record access answer a client can ask for is `can-manage-access` (`RecordAccessGateEndpoint.cs:63-108`), which is Write-gated by the group's `DelegationRuleFilter` (`DelegationRuleFilter.cs:86`) and documents itself as "not a permissions API" (`:27-32`). A Grep of `Api/ExternalAccess` for `MapGet(` finds no access-status route today. 064's UX amendment adds the Read-gated No Access SUMMARY route for root, organization and contact records, but it carries no Secure signal and no record-id echo. (2) Reader: `NoAccessListReader` (`:128-155`) is principal-keyed; 064 adds the record-scoped method this task consumes. (3) Web resource: no authored `setFormNotification` anywhere in src/. The on-load libraries on these forms are KPI-specific (`sprk_matter_kpi_refresh.js`) or assigned-access post-save on three forms only (task 142's `sprk_assignedaccess_postsave.js`). (4) Indicator: TrackingFieldTrio's header row holds only the person and email icons (`TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:253-287`).</existing>
    <extension>(1) Server: extended, not added — 064's SUMMARY route, DTO and composer gain the Secure signal, the closed signal block and the record-id echo; no endpoint, filter, operation key or reader method is added. `can-manage-access` cannot be extended because its Write gate would hide the banner from Read-only viewers. (2) Indicator: extends the existing TrackingFieldTrio component and PCF with one opt-in prop and reuses 067's section-aware open callback; no new control. (3) Web resource: a new thin library, because the form-banner concern spans five forms and no existing library is registered on all of them. A `setFormNotification` banner cannot be produced by a PCF on the form, and ADR-006 permits a thin form event handler.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Read-only attorney opening a secure matter, or a matter that sits behind an ethical wall, gets no signal on the form. The Manage Access modal's Secure line (`AccessGrantModal.tsx:1170-1178`) is behind a person icon that is disabled for them (`TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:248`), and nothing anywhere tells them about the wall. On Organization and Contact forms, entries naming that organization or contact are invisible to everyone except access administrators once O2 removes core users' table Read (0 No Access components today, research note :29). The owner's round-3b banner requirement fails outright.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

