  <escalation>
    <trigger>(O1) OPEN OWNER QUESTION, under owner investigation (research note :75-77) — must the banner itself be clickable? The owner believes OOB notifications can carry links. The findings (background "FORM NOTIFICATION MECHANISMS"; not repo-verified): `setFormNotification` is documented text-only; `Xrm.App.addGlobalNotification` takes a clickable action but is app-wide, persists across navigation with no unload event to clear it, and its handler cannot open AccessGrantModal, which exists only inside the TrackingFieldTrio PCF (`index.ts:1170-1207`); the other candidates do not fit. RECOMMENDATION: BOTH. (1) The standard red `setFormNotification` banner at the top of the form, naming the action and who can take it, visible to every reader. (2) A clickable indicator inside TrackingFieldTrio, the only Manage Access entry point (`TrackingFieldTrio.tsx:253-273`), that opens Manage Access at the No Access section (No Access) or at the top (Secure), clickable only for callers the server says may manage access. Do not use the undocumented fourth `setFormNotification` parameter under any answer (unsupported). If the owner chooses `addGlobalNotification`, record how it is cleared when the user leaves the record (e.g. clear on every OnLoad and check `Xrm.Utility.getPageContext()`), and prove it in the live gate. Also ask the owner to confirm or revise the closed banner copy. STOP before step 4 and step 6 until answered. Steps 2, 3 and 5 may proceed, because the server summary is needed under every answer.</trigger>
    <trigger>(O2) OWNER QUESTION — ANSWERED 2026-10-01: ACCEPTED as recommended (research note :74; task 154 applies it). The question: should the No Access list, including Reason, stay readable by every core user (Global Read on "Spaarke Core User" today)? RECOMMENDATION (accepted): no. Remove Read from Spaarke Core User, grant Read/Write to a dedicated access-administrator role, everyone else sees this task's banner, and Write-holders see the entries through Manage Access (the BFF reads on their behalf). This task's summary is computed server-side after the caller's Read gate, so it works under either answer; only the org/contact copy ("Access administrators manage the entries in the NO ACCESS section") depends on it. At step 0, confirm the note still records ACCEPTED. If it does not, or the owner revises O2, STOP before finalizing that copy and record the revised answer.</trigger>
    <trigger>(c) If 064 has merged WITHOUT the record-scoped No Access read, WITHOUT its Read-gated SUMMARY route, or WITHOUT item (3) (organization and contact records), STOP and report the dependency gap to the orchestrator. Do not build a second deny reader, a second composer or a second summary route here.</trigger>
    <trigger>(d) If the live gate shows that a `setFormNotification` ERROR-level notification does not render as the red form banner on any of the five forms (e.g. suppressed by form configuration), STOP and report it with a screenshot, rather than substituting another surface.</trigger>
    <trigger>(e) If TrackingFieldTrio is NOT on the live main form of project, matter or work assignment, STOP and report which form lacks it. RECOMMENDATION: add the control to that form (it carries Manage Access too), but a form-layout change is the owner's call.</trigger>
    <trigger>(f) ADR/§11 TENSION — the Organization banner's Read gate (CLAUDE.md §6.5). 064 says STOP and escalate before widening the shared map for the organization summary. If 064 has landed a resolution, follow it and record it. Otherwise STOP and present the §6.5 block:
- the rule in question: `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` declares no map of its own (`:58-63`), and `EntityAccessFilter`'s map is held in lockstep with `DocumentAssociationMap` (`:111-122`), which has no organization entry;
- the options:
  (A) a narrowly scoped, documented exception: the summary route alone passes a Read-only `sprk_organization` → `sprk_organizations` resolution to the filter, with a comment citing both invariants;
  (B) amend the lockstep rule so a type can be authorizable for READ without being a document-association target;
  (C) ship the Organization banner later and the other four forms now;
- RECOMMENDATION: (A), recorded as a project-scoped exception in the design and the PR.
Never widen the shared map, never weaken `DelegationRuleFilter`, and never authorize an organization record app-only in place of the caller's gate.</trigger>
    <trigger>(g) If step 1 finds rows whose `sprk_issecure` is NULL on any of the three root tables, STOP and report the counts. Those rows would show "Access status unavailable" permanently, because a NULL read cannot be told apart from a masked one. RECOMMENDATION: a one-time, owner-approved backfill of NULL to false, run by an operator script under an identity that 150's field-level security permits to write the field (no plugin, no flow), with the before/after counts recorded, before the banner is published. Rejected alternative: reading NULL as "not secure", which fails open if the flag is ever masked.</trigger>
  </escalation>

