  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. For a project, matter and work assignment, the response carries exactly `secure` and `noAccessOnRecord`; for an organization exactly `organizationDenied` and `organizationWall`; for a contact exactly `contactDenied` and `contactMemberOfDeniedOrganization`. Every state is one of applies / doesNotApply / unknown. The body echoes the record id. No entry id, subject or object id or name, or reason appears in the body (asserted on the serialized JSON); the only counts present are 064's SUMMARY counts, and neither client renders them. A No Access read fault returns 064's ProblemDetails, never a 200 with `doesNotApply`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Secure tri-state: `sprk_issecure` true → `applies`; false → `doesNotApply`; attribute absent (masked), NULL, row unreturned or read faulted → `unknown`. Each case is tested, and none of the unknown cases yields `applies` or `doesNotApply`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. `noAccessOnRecord`: an active entry whose object record is R → `applies`; an active entry whose object organization is one of R's referenced organizations → `applies`; only inactive or malformed entries → `doesNotApply`; R's referenced organizations unreadable, or a fail-closed deny read → `unknown`. The signal is computed by 064's composer; the notes name the composer method reused; this task adds no method to `NoAccessListReader` (diff); and no class other than `NoAccessListReader` issues a request to `sprk_noaccessentries` (Grep of src/server recorded in the notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. Organization: an active entry with subject organization O → `organizationDenied` applies; an active entry with object organization O → `organizationWall` applies; each kind is independent. Contact: an active entry with subject contact C → `contactDenied` applies; an active entry whose subject organization is one of C's ACTIVE organizations → `contactMemberOfDeniedOrganization` applies (an INACTIVE membership does not count); an unreadable membership → `unknown`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Route authorization, tested THROUGH the real pipeline. A caller with Read but not Write on R gets 200. A caller without Read → 403 ProblemDetails with a reason code, and its detail does not mention adding content. A probe fault → 403. Unauthenticated → 401. A CIAM-scheme token → refused. A request with no caller bearer token is denied, never answered app-only. An unsupported entity type → 403 (not 400). `EntityAccessFilter`'s map is unchanged (diff shows no new entry; its existing tests pass). Organization records are authorized exactly as escalation (f) resolved, with a positive (Read) and a negative (no Read) test for an organization.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. A change takes effect without waiting on a cache: the summary for R reflects an entry added, or the Secure flag changed, immediately before the request (no new cache key is introduced — asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. Web resource, live: on each of the five main forms, every `applies` signal shows its closed-set ERROR notification, with exactly the text and id in the copy constraint (or the owner's revision). `doesNotApply` shows nothing and clears a prior notification with that id. Any `unknown`, a 403/404/500, a missing `Spaarke.BffAuth`, a `null` token or `null` Response from `authenticatedFetch`, an unresolved BFF base URL, or an answer naming another record shows only the INFO unavailable notification (and clears every ERROR id). No text anywhere says "not secure" or "not restricted". No count, name or reason is shown. The form still loads and saves when the script throws.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. The banner re-evaluates after a save (OnPostSave) and after a data refresh (`formContext.data.addOnLoad`): saving an entry, or securing a record through 150's ribbon command, then refreshing, updates the banner without a full page reload. A create form with no record id makes no call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. TrackingFieldTrio indicator (per O1): Secure and/or No Access shown in red, unavailable shown neutral, nothing when every signal is `doesNotApply`. With `canGrantAccess === true`, a No Access click (or a click when both apply) opens AccessGrantModal at 067's No Access section and a Secure-only click opens it at the top, both through 067's section-aware `onOpenGrantModal`. With anything else, or in the unavailable state, there is no click handler and a tooltip says the caller cannot manage access. A consumer that does not pass `accessStatus` renders exactly as before (existing TrackingFieldTrio tests unchanged and green). No second open callback prop exists (types.ts diff).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. The PCF's status fetch follows `evaluateGrantGate`'s rules: every non-200, unparseable body, missing kind or record-id mismatch → unavailable; an answer for a record the control has left is dropped. Component tests cover each.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in criteria 1-10 (tri-state per signal, masked flag, unreadable referenced orgs, inactive and malformed entries, inactive membership, read-tier authorization negatives through the real pipeline, client failure modes, click gating). No criterion is met by a test that only asserts a mock was called with arguments the test itself supplied. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes. No ADR-038-banned shapes. BFF build, full unit suite, ArchTests and the shared-library jest suite are green; `npm run build:prod` succeeds for the PCF. Publish size reported (fresh-master vs fresh-branch, both sizes, delta, zip tool, both file counts) ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE. No plugin or flow.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. MANUAL live gate on spaarkedev1, using existing non-admin test users in their current BUs, with the evidence (screenshots + network captures) recorded:
(i) a Read-only user opens a secure project and sees the SECURE banner; the indicator is not clickable;
(ii) a Write user on a matter with an active entry (object = the matter) sees the NO ACCESS RESTRICTION banner, clicks the indicator, and lands in Manage Access at No Access;
(iii) a work assignment referencing an organization that carries an ethical wall shows the No Access banner;
(iv) an Organization form with an entry naming it as subject, and another naming it as object, shows both banners; a Contact form for a contact named as subject shows its banner;
(v) with the BFF route blocked in the browser dev tools, each form shows ONLY the unavailable notice;
(vi) a Read-only user on the matter in (ii) sees the banner, the indicator is not clickable, and the network capture shows no request to 064's entries route (067 criterion (e));
(vii) after navigating from a secure or walled record to an unrestricted one, no banner from the first record remains (this matters most if O1 chose `addGlobalNotification`);
(viii) dark mode per the ui-tests.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Secure banner for a Read-only viewer">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={secure-project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as an existing non-admin test user who can Read but not Write the secure project</step>
        <step>Open the project form and wait for the form to finish loading</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>A red form notification reads exactly the SECURE RECORD copy; the TrackingFieldTrio indicator shows Secure in red and has no click action (its tooltip says the user cannot manage access here); no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="No Access banner and indicator open Manage Access at No Access">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={walled-matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as a non-admin test user with Write on the matter, which has an active No Access entry naming it</step>
        <step>Verify the NO ACCESS RESTRICTION form notification</step>
        <step>Click the No Access indicator in the tracking panel header</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The banner text matches the closed copy; Manage Access opens directly at the No Access section; the banner names no person, organization or reason.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Organization and Contact banners">
      <steps>
        <step>Open an Organization that is the subject of one active entry and the object of another</step>
        <step>Open a Contact that is the subject of an active entry; then a Contact that is only an active member of a denied organization</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Organization shows both the NO ACCESS and the ETHICAL WALL notifications; the first Contact shows the contact-denied notification; the second shows the member-of-denied-organization notification.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Fail closed: status unavailable">
      <steps>
        <step>In the browser dev tools, block requests to the access-status route</step>
        <step>Reload a secure project form, an Organization form and a Contact form</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each form shows only the neutral "Access status unavailable" INFO notification; the indicator shows the neutral unavailable state; nothing says the record is unrestricted.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Read-only viewer cannot reach the No Access list">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={walled-matter-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as an existing non-admin test user with Read but not Write on the walled matter</step>
        <step>Hover and click the No Access indicator; watch the network tab</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The NO ACCESS RESTRICTION banner shows; the indicator has no click action and its tooltip says the user cannot manage access here; Manage Access does not open; no request is sent to 064's entries route.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="No banner carried to the next record">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a secure project, then navigate within the app to a non-secure project with no No Access entries</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The second form shows no SECURE or NO ACCESS banner and no unavailable notice.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Refresh after an access change">
      <steps>
        <step>On a non-secure work assignment, use 150's Make Secure ribbon command (or deactivate the record's only No Access entry in another tab, then refresh the form)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>After the form's data refresh the banner updates (SECURE appears, or NO ACCESS RESTRICTION disappears) without a full page reload.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the TrackingFieldTrio indicator in a host using a Fluent dark theme (the shared component under its jest render with webDarkTheme, and any React-19 host that consumes it)</step>
        <step>Verify the red and neutral states are legible and use semantic tokens (no hard-coded colours; icons use currentColor)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours resolve from Fluent v9 tokens in light and dark themes.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

